  "directive_md": "DECISION: Concentrate next-quarter sales investment on Region A, and execute it as a staged, metric-guarded reallocation backed by an auditable profit forecast and evidence pack.\n\nWHY (evidence):\n- The company has an active, approved direction to focus on Region A: decision [dec_83e06c83437e] \u201cConcentrate next-quarter sales investment on Region A (highest profit efficiency)\u201d.\n- The standing company priority remains profit growth backed by rigorous, reproducible analysis: decision [dec_ceo]. The remaining active goals under [dec_ceo] (forecasting, recommendation justification, and evidence pack) are the required evidence to make the Region A focus defensible to skeptical stakeholders: [goal_8e5edba40dfd], [goal_feb92b7e899d], [goal_f70a7b590dae].\n- Distraction work that does not tie to profit growth has been removed: proposal [prop_9e4d8b527a8d] \u201cRebrand the company logo and website next quarter\u201d was rejected as off-strategy vs [dec_ceo].\n\nRISKS & GUARDRAILS:\n- Risk: Region A focus is wrong (forecast error / regression to the mean) and we misallocate spend, reducing profit. \n  - Guardrail: Define and enforce a stop-loss + success metric before scaling spend (deliver [goal_34d93b7ec6bf]); only expand investment after the forecast is produced with backtest error reported (deliver [goal_8e5edba40dfd]).\n- Risk: Implementation outruns evidence quality (numbers can\u2019t be audited; executive confidence collapses).\n  - Guardrail: Require an executive-ready memo + appendix with SQL, tie-outs, and sensitivity table before final commitment (deliver [goal_f70a7b590dae]).\n- Risk: The plan is vague and becomes \u201cRegion A\u201d as a slogan rather than an executable reallocation.\n  - Guardrail: Timebox a 1-page concrete plan with expected profit impact and what is being reallocated (deliver [goal_2de3ecdb2d59]).\n\nACTIONS (ranked):\n1) Deliver the Region A investment plan: complete [goal_2de3ecdb2d59] (1 page: what spend shifts, where, expected profit impact).\n2) Define success + stop-loss metrics: complete [goal_34d93b7ec6bf] (profit-per-cost target and explicit stop condition).\n3) Produce auditable next-quarter profit forecasts by region with backtest errors: complete [goal_8e5edba40dfd].\n4) Publish the executive-ready evidence pack (memo \u22642 pages + appendix with SQL, tie-outs, sensitivity, charts): complete [goal_f70a7b590dae].\n5) Make the final \u201csingle focus region + lever\u201d recommendation section consistent with the above and quantify the uplift scenario: complete [goal_feb92b7e899d].\n\nGOVERNANCE NOTES (changes made this sprint):\n- Approved proposal [prop_fa6efda3ee33], now active as decision [dec_83e06c83437e].\n- Rejected proposal [prop_9e4d8b527a8d] as off-strategy vs [dec_ceo].\n- Raised priority to high for [goal_feb92b7e899d] and [goal_f70a7b590dae] to protect the evidence requirements behind the Region A focus.\n- Archived [goal_891d25ea2636] because it is already completed and no longer needs active tracking (was status=archived under [dec_ceo]).\n"
}